mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Video Platform Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister backs a YouTube-style video application: a newest-first home feed, a trending list ranked by view count, category browsing for viral game and entertainment content, video upload and playback metadata, likes, saves, follows, creator profiles with avatars, and a coin balance that can be topped up through Stripe card checkout.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nEvery method that reads or writes a user's own data derives the caller from the authenticated principal supplied by the Internet Computer. The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nRead-only feed methods (`listFeed`, `listTrending`, `listByCategory`, `getVideo`, `getProfile`, `listCoinPacks`) are public queries and accept anonymous callers. Methods that read the caller's own data (`getMyProfile`, `listMyVideos`, `listMySaved`, `getMyCoinBalance`, `isFollowing`) and every mutation (`createVideo`, `incrementViewCount`, `updateMyProfile`, `toggleFollow`, `toggleLike`, `toggleSave`, `creditMyCoins`, `createCoinCheckout`, `confirmCoinPurchase`) require a signed, non-anonymous caller. A caller's own profile is created lazily on first read or write; there is no separate registration step.\n\nStripe configuration methods (`isStripeConfigured`, `setStripeConfiguration`) are provided by the Stripe mixin. `setStripeConfiguration` is admin-only; `isStripeConfigured` is a public query.\n\n## Authorization\n\nAll mutations are authorized to the caller only. A signed-in user can modify only their own profile, likes, saves, follows and coin balance. Video ownership is recorded at creation and cannot be reassigned. A different signed-in user cannot modify another user's videos, saved list, follows or profile. Coin purchases credit only the caller who started the checkout session.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- `VideoId` is a `Nat` assigned sequentially by the canister.\n- `UserId` is a `Principal`.\n- `Timestamp` (`createdAt`) is an `Int` in nanoseconds since the Unix epoch, as returned by `Time.now()`.\n- `FileRef` is a `Text` reference to an uploaded object (video file or thumbnail).\n- `Category` is a variant with exactly two tags: `#game` and `#entertainment`.\n- `avatar` is an optional `FileRef`; `null` means no avatar is set.\n- `coinBalance` is a non-negative `Nat`.\n- `CoinPack.priceInCents` is the Stripe charge in the smallest currency unit (USD cents); `CoinPack.coins` is the number of coins credited on a successful purchase. `CoinPack.currency` is a lowercase ISO currency code such as `usd`.\n\n## Coin purchase flow\n\n1. `listCoinPacks()` returns the fixed catalogue of purchasable packs (id, name, description, coins, priceInCents, currency).\n2. `createCoinCheckout(packId, successUrl, cancelUrl)` starts a Stripe checkout session for the signed-in caller and returns the raw Stripe session JSON, which includes a `url` to redirect the browser to. Coins are **not** credited at this step. It traps if Stripe is not configured or the pack id is unknown.\n3. After the user completes payment and returns to `successUrl`, the frontend calls `confirmCoinPurchase(sessionId, packId)`. This checks the session status with Stripe and, only when the payment has completed, credits the pack's coins to the caller and returns the new balance.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- `createVideo` returns the created `VideoView` immediately; the video is visible in `listFeed` and `listMyVideos` on the next query.\n- `incrementViewCount` is fire-and-forget and returns `()`; it silently does nothing when the video id does not exist.\n- `toggleLike` and `toggleSave` return the new boolean state (`true` = liked/saved). Poll `getVideo` or `listMySaved` to observe the resulting counts and lists.\n- `toggleFollow` returns the new following state and updates both the follower's and the creator's counts.\n- `creditMyCoins` returns the new balance.\n- `createCoinCheckout` returns the Stripe session JSON; the caller must redirect to its `url` and then poll `confirmCoinPurchase` after payment. `confirmCoinPurchase` returns the caller's current balance.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `toggleLike`, `toggleSave` and `toggleFollow` are **not idempotent**: each call flips the current state. Retrying a call whose response was lost reverses the intended change. Read the current state first (`getVideo`, `isFollowing`) before retrying.\n- `incrementViewCount` is additive and not idempotent; a retry increments the count again.\n- `createVideo` is not idempotent; a retry creates a second video with a new id.\n- `updateMyProfile` is idempotent: it sets the display name and avatar to the supplied values.\n- `creditMyCoins` is additive and not idempotent; a retry credits the amount again.\n- `createCoinCheckout` is not idempotent; a retry creates a second Stripe checkout session. Only the session the user actually pays is credited.\n- `confirmCoinPurchase` is **idempotent per session id**: each completed session is credited at most once, so polling it repeatedly is safe and returns the same balance after the first successful credit. A session that has not completed yet traps with `Payment did not complete`; retry after the payment settles.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- `getVideo` and `getProfile` return `null` for an unknown id rather than trapping.\n- `toggleLike` returns `false` when the video does not exist; `toggleFollow` returns `false` when the caller tries to follow themselves.\n- `listMySaved` returns only videos that still exist; saved entries for deleted videos are skipped.\n- `getMyProfile` creates an empty profile on first call, so it never returns an error for a signed-in caller.\n- `createCoinCheckout` and `confirmCoinPurchase` trap when Stripe has not been configured by an admin, and `createCoinCheckout` traps for an unknown pack id.\n- `confirmCoinPurchase` traps with `Payment did not complete` when the Stripe session has failed or is still pending; it does not credit coins in that case.\n- Feed and trending lists are returned in full; there is no server-side pagination.\n";
  };
};
